# Same list as .gitignore, and for the same reason: running the binary from
# here leaves an instance's files in the working copy, and the build context is
# another way for one of them to leave the machine. The Dockerfile copies named
# directories rather than the whole context, so this is the second lock on a
# door that is already shut — which is what you want on the door that was
# already left open once.
*.key
*.pem
*.log
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
